y  care about those issues but they care  far more about the issue of whether or  not donald trump is president  and an astonishing 90 percent of voters  according to polls  have already made up their mind about  who they're voting for there's not a lot  of room to pick up new supporters  tonight  although arguably both men will be  trying to do that really the polls have  been consistent in biden's favor he's  maintained a six to eight point lead  for three or four months now those  numbers haven't budged donna  voters are really locked in at this  point i'm always skeptical of the polls  though especially after last time and  jackson  this campaign and this whole year has  been flooded with misinformation  conspiracy theories lies and stuff is  spreading about this debate  before it's even started tell us about  that yeah these are rumors that tend to  come up around  every debate but they're specific to  this one in the sense that donald trump  has put a lot of effort into claiming  that joe biden is in some sort of mental  decline that of course is a baseless  conspiracy theory  but now it seems like the trump campaign  is worried that biden might actually  perform well this evening so they're  spreading the rumor that  perhaps he's taking  performance-enhancing drugs or wearing  some sort of earpiece to feed him in the  answers  donna that is all baseless but it gives  you a sense of the information war  that's going to surround an event that  has a super bowl sized audience  all right we will be watching jackson  prosco in washington thanks  another province is having a pandemic  election coming up  what's at stake in saskatchewan  voters in saskatchewan are heading to  the polls on october 26th  it's the third province to hold an  election in the midst of the pandemic  premier scott mo took over the  leadership of the saskatchewan party  from brad wall in 2018 so this will be  his first crack  at getting elected as premier ryan  kessler is with me from saskatoon ryan  what kind of campaign  is expected donna the governing  saskatchewan party is asking voters who  they trust to lead the economic recovery  coming out of the covet 19 pandemic  as you mentioned it's scott moe's first  race as leader but he's relying on his  party's track record over the course of  the last 13 years  while attacking the opposition ndp  according to mo the sask party has  the right plan to make life more  affordable in saskatchewan while  balancing the budget by 2024.  he says the province's ndp and leader  ryan miley would go on a spending spree  if elected  he wants to spend with no no plan of  balance no plan to grow  the economy here in the province which  ultimately means  that there will be cuts at some time in  the future when this type of reckless  spending  is allowed to to occur of the  legislature's 61 seats 46 are held by  the sask party  13 belong to the new democrats and two  are vacant  the ndp is positioning itself as the  party that will invest in the people  files  such as education and health care the  ndp's tone is similar to what it was  during the 2016 election  accusing the sask party of planning cuts  instead of investments  and if they're re-elected it will only  be worse austerity  on steroids on day one of this campaign  both parties were light on platform  specifics but heavy on political  rhetoric  there's still plenty of time for those  details before voters head to the polls  with pandemic precautions on october  26th  donna all right ryan kessler in  saskatoon tonight thanks  virus detector next the canadian  technology putting hope  in the air  a company in southwestern ontario claims  to have developed game-changing  technology in the fight against covet  19.  it's designed a wall-mounted device that  looks similar to a carbon monoxide  detector  it scans the air for covet 19 particles  the devices  aren't in use yet they're still in the  testing phase and they're not cheap the  cost is about twelve thousand 